WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:06.640
“They came from beyond the world, from&nbsp;
over the world, from under the world.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.280
They came from inside the&nbsp;
stars and from behind the rain.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:16.720
They came from the known lands and they&nbsp;
came from the secret places of old.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:22.800
The vast ones who drank of the nebulae, the small&nbsp;
ones who did not care what happened beyond the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:29.520
banks of their rivers, the ones who bathed in the&nbsp;
light and the ones who watched from the shadows,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:33.680
the ones who loved us and&nbsp;
the ones who forgot about us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:40.480
the ones who hate us now and the ones who love&nbsp;
us still, the ones who sung with the rats and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:48.640
the ones who swam with the leviathans, they&nbsp;
came from far and near, they came one and all.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.520
They came to end the world.”

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:55.760
As you may already know from our previous&nbsp;
video in this series, a mysterious being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.760 --> 00:01:02.400
known only as the Harbinger unlocked SCP-001 -&nbsp;
The Lock - and brought about the Omnipocalypse:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.320
Every single world-destroying&nbsp;
XK Class Scenario on the books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.960
from Foundation files to the most ancient&nbsp;
mythological tomes, and some we’d never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:16.880
even imagined, began to come true. A world&nbsp;
flooded with terrifying anomalous activity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:22.080
from unfurling skies to giant, nightmarish&nbsp;
animals, was about where we left off.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.120
Now it’s time to open your eyes and wake up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:29.360
This is the kind of nightmare you&nbsp;
can’t encounter when you’re asleep.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:34.800
SCP-5720, the Astronomically-Inclined&nbsp;
Crane, went about its daily work.&nbsp;

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:39.040
The small mechanical crane always occupied&nbsp;
itself with the one task that gave its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:43.840
existence any meaning: Arranging&nbsp;
esoteric model solar systems. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:49.760
something was different today. SCP-5720 put&nbsp;
the final touches on its latest model, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:56.000
then lifted its mechanical arm skywards, pointing&nbsp;
directly into the vast and starry infinity above.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:02.560
But were they stars? No, not today.&nbsp;
As SCP-5720 looked up at the sky,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:09.040
this time, the sky looked back.&nbsp;
They weren’t stars: They were eyes.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:13.680
Something was coming towards earth from&nbsp;
the furthest reaches of the outer dark.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.960
An armada of world-enders. Coming from above,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:25.280
below, and all around, a whole cosmos of supremely&nbsp;
powerful beings, zeroing in on our pale blue dot.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:29.600
A thought crossed through whatever passed&nbsp;
as the mind of this strange little crane:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:34.960
“Today is the day your prayers will be answered.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:41.080
Followed by another word, ringing loud and clear&nbsp;
and holy as a mighty church bell: “AWAKEN.”

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:47.120
And at that moment, everything did.
Thousands of miles away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:53.600
a new God landed on earth, appearing like a great&nbsp;
wall of dense, matted fur descending from the sky.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:59.680
Ur-An-Uum, the mother of the ones that&nbsp;
came before. After eons of absence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:03.920
she had eventually returned to greet&nbsp;
her children, the true rulers and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:09.440
stewards of this land. But Ur-An-Uum was&nbsp;
surprised and horrified by what she saw.

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:12.560
Their great cities, their sprawling structures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:18.960
their beautiful art, and advanced culture...All&nbsp;
gone. Laid to waste by the worthless hairless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:24.800
apes that once lurked in the forests with the&nbsp;
other animals. Something had happened, something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.360 --> 00:03:31.120
had...changed. The humans had slaughtered&nbsp;
her people. Destroyed their accomplishments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.800
Tarnished their legacy. Driven the few that were&nbsp;
left out of their kingdoms and into the forests;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.240
treated them as mere animals, and built their&nbsp;
hideous concrete cities over their bones.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:47.120
And they had the gall to call&nbsp;
them “Bigfoot”, or SCP-1000,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:53.200
because thanks to them, their beautiful true&nbsp;
name had been lost to time. She looked skywards&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:58.560
and cried out in despair and anguish at the&nbsp;
loss of her children, inconsolable. But then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:04.640
she felt something - A glimmer of hope in her&nbsp;
mind, the possibility that things would change.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:10.080
That the humans would be toppled from their&nbsp;
thrones and true justice would be achieved.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.960
She called out to her remaining&nbsp;
children, and her children answered.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:20.160
Across the globe, another great entity awoke,&nbsp;
deep underneath a mountain. When it stirred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:25.280
into life and broke free, it shattered the&nbsp;
entire mountain on top of it, as easily as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:31.920
you or me displacing a bedsheet. It took to the&nbsp;
skies, massive but unseeable to the human eye.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.200
It soared through the air, gazing down upon the&nbsp;
world it hadn’t seen for thousands of years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:42.320
Once it had feasted on the blood sacrifices&nbsp;
of human subjects hoping to avoid its wrath,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:46.960
but humans weren’t the petty little group&nbsp;
of huddled cavemen that they had once been.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:52.320
Now, they were in their billions, gathered in&nbsp;
impossibly large settlements. The Entity sought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:58.400
to find a seat of power that it could influence,&nbsp;
but now, it was spoiled for choice. Eventually,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:04.320
it zeroed in and found its perfect target:&nbsp;
An SCP Foundation containment site. Here,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:10.160
it would find a new form to take, and more petty,&nbsp;
pathetic humans to bring under its mighty thrall.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:16.560
It landed in SCP-765, the Duck Pond.
It’s an anomalous pond that is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:22.000
you guessed it, full of ducks, and initially&nbsp;
induces feelings of serenity in its victims,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:27.360
before later inducing not so pleasant feelings.&nbsp;
When The Entity plummeted into the water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:32.880
it began to absorb and bond with the anomaly,&nbsp;
growing to epic sizes as it assumed a form&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.640
that the minds of us feeble humans could&nbsp;
comprehend: A giant, terrifying duck.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.960
It released a mighty, earth-shaking quack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:44.720
as it plodded across the countryside&nbsp;
to cause mayhem elsewhere.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:50.800
In Europe, more violent madness was unfolding.&nbsp;
A crimson rooster cawed, then a golden rooster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.760
and then a rooster of soot-red. Anyone with&nbsp;
a basic knowledge of Norse mythology was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.760 --> 00:06:00.400
shaking in their boots as a mighty beast&nbsp;
stirred in the heart of a desolate cave.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.400
The chains that had once held the&nbsp;
monstrous dog in place now broke.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:09.920
It rose and licked its jagged fangs, excited&nbsp;
to stain them with the blood of its enemies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:16.880
It was the Great Hound Fenrir, Omen of the End&nbsp;
Times, here to herald the end of all things.&nbsp;

00:06:16.880 --> 00:06:20.640
A trumpet boomed across the&nbsp;
globe, with no apparent source.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:26.480
People in the streets in New York, Delhi, London,&nbsp;
Cape Town, and countless other towns, cities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:33.040
and hamlets the world over paused and listened&nbsp;
in confusion. Below them, the great and terrible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.040 --> 00:06:38.480
Jörmungandr - the thought-to-be-mythological&nbsp;
Midgard serpent - stirred from its previously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:44.080
eternal slumber and began to uncoil its body.&nbsp;
The shifting caused earthquakes and tsunamis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.080 --> 00:06:48.800
along the coast of Greenland, as towns&nbsp;
and villages crumbled, killing thousands.&nbsp;

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.200
Fenrir stalked across the length of Denmark,&nbsp;
slaughtering and devouring anyone or anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:58.480
unlucky enough to cross its path. But it&nbsp;
did not wage its war against mankind alone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:04.720
Behind it, a hellish army of burning giants&nbsp;
marched, mighty hands clutching molten weapons.

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:08.720
Ragnarok was upon us now. Odin save us all.

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.920
And The Administrator...Slept. She was the&nbsp;
latest in a long line of Foundation staff&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:18.640
members to hold that hallowed position,&nbsp;
and in the dark vistas of her dreams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:23.920
a predecessor approached her. He wasn’t the old,&nbsp;
bearded man in a heavy coat that she remembered.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:28.800
Now, he was wearing a 1950s suit and a&nbsp;
fedora hat, and carrying a briefcase.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:35.040
That’s right - He’d taken up the mantle&nbsp;
of SCP-990, also known as The Dream Man.&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.360
He’s a mysterious figure that appears to&nbsp;
members of the Foundation in their dreams,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:44.000
warning them of impending disasters that they&nbsp;
may be able to narrowly prevent if his warning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:49.040
is heeded. Though it often comes at some&nbsp;
terrible cost to the recipient of his message.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:52.480
This time, however, his message&nbsp;
carried a different tone:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:56.160
He told the current administrator that&nbsp;
there was no way to stop the apocalypse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.080
from occurring this time, only making&nbsp;
sure that the particular shape of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:06.000
apocalypse would be the one most favorable to&nbsp;
the Foundation and humanity’s joint interests.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:10.800
All this was devastating news that the new&nbsp;
Administrator saw as a grievous betrayal of both&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:16.480
the Foundation’s stances and humanity as a whole.&nbsp;
She refused to accept the idea that the apocalypse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:22.320
was inevitable, even coming from the mouth of a&nbsp;
former Administrator. As far as she was concerned,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:25.680
this Dream Man no longer worked&nbsp;
on the side of the Foundation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:30.320
He was in league with the world enders,&nbsp;
and she refused to take his deal.

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:34.560
The SCP Foundation would save this world&nbsp;
from the horrors the Lock unleashed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:40.080
or they would slide into the darkness with it.&nbsp;
They would never work against the human race.

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:47.280
SCP-343, also known as God, awoke in his cell&nbsp;
in Site-17. The time for fun and games with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:52.960
humans at the Foundation had come and gone,&nbsp;
he was going by his true name, Yahweh, now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.960 --> 00:09:00.080
He blinked, and in that same instant, he was at&nbsp;
Site 0 - The containment site for another SCP-001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.080 --> 00:09:05.280
the legendary Gate Guardian. All the staff&nbsp;
around them looked upon Yahweh in shock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:09.760
awed by the reality warper’s sudden&nbsp;
appearance and unable to do anything about it.

00:09:09.760 --> 00:09:12.800
But really, 343 was no mere reality warper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:20.160
like some had expected. 343 truly was a God - He&nbsp;
just didn’t happen to be the only one in play.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:23.200
When the Gate Guardian saw&nbsp;
Yahweh now standing before him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:28.720
he lowered his sword, spread his fiery&nbsp;
wings, and took a knee in great reverence.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:32.160
Yahweh spoke calmly, but&nbsp;
with unshakable authority.

00:09:32.760 --> 00:09:39.680
“Uriel, it is Time. Open the Gate.&nbsp;
Lead My armies across the Earth.”

00:09:40.480 --> 00:09:52.800
The Gate Guardian, Uriel, responded in its booming&nbsp;
voice: “I HEAR AND OBEY, MY LORD AND MY GOD.”

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:59.040
For the first time in recorded memory, the grand&nbsp;
gate that Uriel had always been guarding opened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.040 --> 00:10:05.200
revealing thousands of legions of warrior angels&nbsp;
waiting on the other side. They were impossibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:11.120
beautiful and powerful creatures. Each one&nbsp;
a vibrant, glowing chaos of wings and eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:16.480
wielding pure white swords and singing&nbsp;
resounding hymns of war. Soon, the air was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:22.080
thick with the chorus of rustling wings, as the&nbsp;
angels loosed themselves from the Gate’s mouth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.080 --> 00:10:26.080
led by Uriel as Yawhweh’s&nbsp;
general, into the global fray.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:32.480
Meanwhile, back at Site 10, another&nbsp;
SCP-001, the item that started all this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:38.720
The Lock, was entering its next stage of grand&nbsp;
cosmic evolution. Something within the lock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:43.920
suddenly unfurled, causing a shockwave that&nbsp;
killed everyone at the site and destroyed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:49.680
the entire building in an instant. Except in&nbsp;
that same instant, all of the Site 10 Staff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.680 --> 00:10:54.880
and the building itself, reappeared completely&nbsp;
unharmed in a field in New Hampshire.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:11:00.080
Back where Site 10 used to be, The Lock was&nbsp;
doing some terraforming. The ground split&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:00.080 --> 00:11:05.840
open beneath it into a mighty valley, the likes of&nbsp;
which Earth had never seen before. Lush greenery&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.840 --> 00:11:12.480
sprouted within, and thousands of strange, alien&nbsp;
creatures soon populated this new place. In the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:18.960
center, The Lock just floated in place. They were&nbsp;
now ready for the first meeting to take place.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:25.760
Over at Site 2036, Dr. Everett Mann was&nbsp;
working on a number of SCP-098 specimens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.960
These are frightening creatures&nbsp;
reminiscent of spider crabs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:33.840
with blades instead of pincers and a natural&nbsp;
ability to mimic the sounds of their prey.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.840 --> 00:11:38.800
He was studying the creatures when he got a call,&nbsp;
asking him if the specimens had acted up at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:44.160
They’d already had sudden containment&nbsp;
breaches for SCP-995, a type of dangerous,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:50.880
carnivorous fungi, and SCP-616, a mysterious&nbsp;
airplane with Satanic elements to it.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:56.800
Just as Dr. Mann was about to reply, the 098&nbsp;
specimens metamorphosed into many-winged flying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.800 --> 00:12:00.800
creatures, which flew out of the chamber&nbsp;
with such force that they busted through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:06.000
walls. Sirens blared all over the facility,&nbsp;
and Dr. Mann joined the many other confused&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.200
and frustrated Foundation staff&nbsp;
members wandering the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:13.600
wondering just what the hell was going on&nbsp;
today. They were getting bizarre reports of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.600 --> 00:12:19.360
unprecedented anomalous activity from all over&nbsp;
the world, with no explanation uniting it all.

00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.240
According to panicked&nbsp;
whispers across the facility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.240 --> 00:12:27.040
Emergency Order Patmos was now in effect,&nbsp;
whatever that meant. The true nature of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:31.840
what was going on here went over most of&nbsp;
the heads of the SCP Foundation’s staff.

00:12:31.840 --> 00:12:37.120
That’s when Mann encountered Dr. Charles Ogden&nbsp;
Gears, who - for such a famously emotionless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:41.840
man - looked surprisingly worried. Dr.&nbsp;
Mann tried to downplay the situation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.840 --> 00:12:44.960
saying they were only looking at a&nbsp;
handful of containment breaches here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:50.240
Nothing they hadn’t handled before. Dr.&nbsp;
Gears shut him down with trademark coldness.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:55.040
Feeling a little more nervous now, Dr.&nbsp;
Everett Mann asked what else had gotten out.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:13:00.400
With steely eyes, Dr. Gears&nbsp;
replied: “A whole damn lot.”

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:08.880
Now go check out “Children of SCP-001 The Scarlet&nbsp;
King - Is SCP-999 Really His Son?” and “SCP-001&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:15.760
Ouroboros Cycle - The Full Story Compilation”&nbsp;
for more interesting explorations into SCP-001!

